From 3d6853b32c7c872df00d9e3489f642dc22e974e000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pondzikk <142788369+pondzikk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:09:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Bugfix] Seed hybrid mamba state index with mamba_block_size
 on prefix-cache hits (#55601)

Verbatim cherry-pick of upstream commit 3d6853b32 (PR #55601, merged to
main 2026-10-07 — after the v0.31.1rc0 tag of 2026-10-06, so in NEITHER
v0.31.0 nor v0.31.1rc0; expected in the v0.31.1 final). Closes #55600.

This is the upstream, merged form of our carried #53798 fix (co-authored
here) and REPLACES 53798-mamba-align-resume-seed.patch. The #53798
version seeded the align state block from MambaSpec.block_size via a
set_kv_cache_config hook; #55601 seeds from
cache_config.mamba_block_size directly. The two are numerically
identical in every current geometry: MambaSpec.block_size is
constructed from cache_config.mamba_block_size
(mamba/abstract.py get_kv_cache_spec), and
unify_kv_cache_spec_page_size PADS the mamba page (page_size_padded)
without scaling MambaSpec.block_size, so the #53798 premise that page
unification scales it past the scheduler block does not hold in
v0.31.x code (ours: align mode, all groups 1600 — both compute the same
column). #55601 additionally hard-asserts mamba_block_size is not None
(cannot fire: MambaSpec construction asserts the same field). Dropping
the #53798 hook machinery (interface.py set_kv_cache_config, eager spec
binding in model_runner.py, _get_mamba_group_info rework) is the payoff.

Re-verified `git apply` clean on VLLM_REF=v0.31.0 (current pin, full
ordered apply + py_compile in scratch clone) and v0.31.1rc0,
2026-10-07.

Drop when a pinned VLLM_REF contains 3d6853b32.

